# =============================================================================
# FRONTEND ENVIRONMENT - TEMPLATE
# =============================================================================
# Copy to `.env.local` for local overrides:
#     cp .env.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local` is gitignored; this template is committed, because a list of the
# variables an app needs is documentation.
#
# !! EVERYTHING HERE IS PUBLIC !!
# Vite substitutes VITE_* variables as string literals into the bundle that is
# served to every browser. There is no such thing as a private value in a
# frontend build. API keys, signing secrets and database URLs belong on the
# NestJS side, and the browser asks the backend to use them on its behalf.
# The VITE_ prefix is a guard rail against accidental exposure, not a security
# boundary.
# =============================================================================

# The API base path.
#
# LEAVE THIS UNSET for normal local development. The default is the RELATIVE
# path `/api/v1`, which the Vite dev proxy forwards to localhost:3000 and which
# nginx reverse-proxies in production. One relative path, correct in both,
# no CORS, and cookies attach automatically.
#
# Set it only to point a local frontend at a REMOTE backend - e.g. staging:
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://staging.example.com/api/v1
# Doing so makes requests cross-origin, so that origin must appear in the
# backend's CORS_ORIGINS allow-list.
#
# The `/api` and `/v1` segments are BOTH required: the backend sets a global
# prefix of `api` and enables URI versioning with defaultVersion '1'.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1
